==================================================\n\n(deftest gensym-test\n  (testing \"a fresh id from the engine's counter, on the stack\"\n    (let [done (run-segment [[:gensym \"id\"] [:halt]])]\n      (is (= :id-0 (vm/value done)))\n      (is (= 1 (:id-counter done)))))\n  (testing \"the counter advances per mint, and a :push after each keeps it\"\n    (is (= :g-2 (vm/value (run-segment [[:gensym \"g\"] [:push] [:gensym \"g\"] [:push]\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/continuation_invoke_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_ffi_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_parity_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_engine_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/code_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/parity_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/link_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/walker_trace_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/load_paths_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/analysis_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/linearize_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_register/vm_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_stream_observer_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc\n   for an arbitrary register payload (`yin.vm.engine.md` section 7, edit 3).\n\n   `entry` is a wait, ready, or parked record as the VM built it: the\n   writer entry that retried the request, or the registers of a call whose\n   request was sent at once. The FFI keys of the writer step\n   (`:request-sent`, `:op`) and its retried `:datom` are removed; the\n   call-out reader keys are added. Every other key -- the VM's register\n   payload, whatever its shape -- is preserved verbatim, so no VM has to\n   know this layout. `call-response-wait-entry` (the walker's frame-typed\n   shape) is unchanged.\"\n  [entry call-id]\n  (-> entry\n      (dissoc :value :status :cursor :resource-updates :stream\n              :datom :type :id :request-sent :op)\n      (assoc :call-id call-id\n             :reason :next\n             :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id vm/call-out-cursor-key}\n2:  \"The request/response envelope for DaoStream v2.\n77:(defn success-response\n78:  \"Construct a successful response preserving the request id.\"\n83:(defn error-response\n84:  \"Construct an error response preserving the request id.\"\n89:(defn response?\n90:  \"True when value is a valid response envelope.  A response contains exactly\n100:(defn response-id\n105:(defn response-ok\n110:(defn response-error\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
