{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,95p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; sed -n '1620,1660p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; rg -n '\"'^##|''^###'\"' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md docs/design/yin.vm.ucf.md docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md | head -65; cat collab/6cpre-mutations.log\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time repo-wide.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time repo-wide to avoid contention.\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n\n### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n\n`bb test:sub <subsystem>...` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the tests belonging to\none or more canonical subsystems (defined in `src/dev/subsystems.edn`). Selection\nis by longest namespace prefix matching.\nclauses above: the export-recovery object's version-1 format\n(`:1789-1807`), which is phase 7's to re-base on the row carrier and is\nnamed in §8.4 as an entry condition, not amended here; publication\nfailure recovery (`:1741`), completion recovery (`:2417`) and the\nledger's \"legacy destructive readers\" (`:2774-2775`), which concern the\ndriver, the ledger protocol and the ledger reader, not a body version,\nand are untouched; and the status paragraph `:39-42`, covered by the\nscope statement's \"every clause\".\n\n### 10.4 To code-as-tuples (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`) §7.2\n\n**C1 (ACCEPT).** Replace the first paragraph with: \"The vector-to-datoms\nprojection path is **retired** (owner ruling 2026-09-18; frozen §3.4\n'One vector validator'). There is one load path for a vector, the direct\none, and two AST projection lanes (datom lane, row lane) that produce\nthe vector; all three feed one validator\n(`yin.vm.semantic-register.code/well-formed?`). UCF §7.3.4's projection\npath is superseded accordingly.\" Replace obligation 2's second sentence\nwith \"loading the vector produced by either AST lane and the vector\nloaded directly yield the same image and address (`load_paths_test.cljc`)\",\nand obligation 3's \"both paths refuse with the same defect\" with \"the\ndirect vector load refuses with the published defect (rule and pc) for\nevery rule of the frozen §3.4\". Obligations 1 and 4 stand.\n\n### 10.5 Checked and consistent (no amendment)\n\nFrozen §2.4 delivery shapes against the 4b branch; frozen §4.1 two state\ncolumns; the evaluator design §1.3-1.6; the draft's §3, §4, §5.1 (except\n`:reified`), §5.3, §6, §7 and §8 steps 1-6, 8-12; v2 amendment §2's `E`\nshape; the phase-5 §9.2 `:yin.k/trees` text; the register kernel's\n`:return-result` delivery (`register.cljc:458-468`).\n\n---\n\n## 11. Owner questions\n\n**None.** The reviewer accepted the engine-less profile and rejected the\nmerged-`E` free environment; both are now settled in the text. Nothing\nremaining is owner-level.\n\n---\nrg: docs/design/yin.vm.ucf.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:36:## 1. Stance, in the owner's words\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:83:## 2. The machine\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:85:### 2.1 Configuration\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:111:### 2.2 Registers\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:122:### 2.3 Instruction table\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:161:### 2.4 Transitions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:325:### 2.5 Correspondence with the walker\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:351:## 3. The canonical grammar\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:353:### 3.1 Expression-structured by construction\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:455:### 3.2 Exclusive definitions by structured paths\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:470:### 3.3 The lowering walk and the minting order\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:543:### 3.4 Well-formedness\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:618:## 4. Safepoints and the continuation format\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:620:### 4.1 The safepoint table (UCF §7.4.1, rewritten)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:661:### 4.2 The UCF frame\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:726:### 4.3 Foreign engines (UCF §7.4.2)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:755:## 5. Scheduler, park, resume, FFI, modules\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:768:## 6. Contract stamp and versions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:787:## 7. What A is, restated\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:804:## 8. Derivations from A\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:810:### 8.1 Static facts per pc: def, use, live\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:839:### 8.2 A → R: the de Bruijn register image\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:934:### 8.3 A → H: the de Bruijn stack image\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:952:### 8.4 Verification\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:974:## 9. Blast radius\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:1019:## 10. Migration\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:1119:## 11. Questions resolved by the freeze review\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md:1143:## 12. What this does not change\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:41:## 1. Stance\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:69:## 2. Positioning: body version 3, one profile\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:81:## 3. Rows, id spaces, and the census\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:178:## 4. The value union\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:250:## 5. The row table\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:272:### 5.1 Values (content rows)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:295:### 5.2 Frame rows: states, windows, waits, frames (content rows)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:321:### 5.3 Pending (content rows)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:357:### 5.4 Task context (content rows)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:390:### 5.5 The root\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:449:## 6. Canonical cell numbering\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:599:## 7. Equality and the content address\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:618:## 8. Validation on lower\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:728:## 9. Lift, lower, and the laws\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:767:## 10. Questions the review answered, and what remains\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:849:## 11. What this does not change\n1 tail-park-is-marked 1 NAMED FAILURE\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
